AsmEdit report

The AsmEdit project has completed another
milestone and now contains:

 * AsmLib a partially completed library
   with about 80 functions.
 * Integrated reference with kernel, x86,
   library, and other information.
 * Editor optimized for assembler.
 * Hooks for compiling, debugging,
   comparing, and manipulating source
   files.

The intent is to create a IDE for assembler
code.

All code is in assembler and AsmEdit is
actively coding itself.  The source
and binaries are at:

http://members.save-net.com/jko%40save-net.com/asm

Any feature requests or comments are welcome.  The
next phase will attempt to create a friendly wrapper
that sets up projects and acts as a file manager.

This project is still in early "alpha" state and
anyone wanting to help or integrate there favorite
assembler can find the project on sourceforge.

